  "case_notes": [
    "Bypass at event-stream@3.3.5 is NOT_COMPUTED: the previous release (3.3.4) is more than 730 days earlier, so the remembered normal has expired (a two-year gap).",
    "event-stream@3.3.6, the malicious release, was removed from the registry: its time is recorded, its publisher and path are not, so Bypass cannot judge it.",
    "The Bypass FIRED at 4.0.0 compares it with a normal of one release, 3.3.5, which was itself the new publisher's first. It fires because 4.0.0 differs from that one release on publisher_in_set, not because it differs from the original maintainer's history.",
    "The first NOTE is therefore after the malicious release; the earlier points are HOLD (one move fired, another unknown)."
  ],
  "honesty": [
    "One real incident per case is too few to claim precision (spec §10.2).",
    "Published as measured: a result that fired late, or not at all, is shown as it was.",
    "Rush: the registry records no grant event. A GRANTED edge is placed at the first version that lists the maintainer, which for a newcomer is also their first release, so days-to-grant is 0 by construction of the record. A Rush FIRED here is an effect of that record, not independent evidence.",
    "Lone keeper counts commit authors in the trailing 90 days; npm data has no commits, so only the guardians half of the flag can be set."
  ],
